          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The <strong class="text-white">best grass seed</strong> is the one matched to your climate first and your light conditions second. For most cool-season lawns, <strong class="text-white">Scotts Turf Builder Sun & Shade Mix</strong> is the sensible default. For a lawn that survives August without irrigation, <strong class="text-white">Jonathan Green Black Beauty Ultra</strong> and its deep fescue roots are worth the premium. And for Southern heat, <strong class="text-white">Scotts Turf Builder Bermudagrass</strong> is the only category that makes sense.
          </p>
